							In DevOps and backend engineering, reversing line sequences is an indispensable daily task. Server debug outputs, Apache access logs, and <code class="rounded bg-canvas px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[12px] text-ink">git log</code> entries are traditionally appended chronologically from oldest to newest. By pasting thousands of log lines into Wordora and toggling <strong class="font-medium text-ink">Line Order</strong>, developers can instantly place the newest incident events at the top of the file without altering timestamps or stack traces inside each row.
